+shapes in varied orientations, moves them between varied source/anchor locations,
+and uses one to three colors. The exact public controls are `grid_h`, `grid_w`,
+`blob_cells`, and `blob_colors`; unknown, coercible, negative, or out-of-range
+values are rejected. A three-profile schedule continuously teaches non-fixed
+orientation, non-origin placement, and monochrome behavior.
+
+The reusable `workspace/lesson_probe.py` independently checks canonical Python
+semantics, protected-Racket parity, and every query rotation against
+`fixed_orientation_L`, `fixed_source_origin`, and `monochrome_object` rivals.
+Retained results cover 72 lesson windows, 288 query rotations, 93 unique
+protected-Racket labels, 15 normalized shapes, 59 source origins, object sizes
+3–7, and color counts 1–3, with zero findings.
+
+Final task tests pass 54/54 and the standalone defect-lint stage passes against
+generator SHA-256
+`b1562c011c136deb1dc30efe4df6df4829dcc75fecd6b48f3a14d8c0c9b54973`.
+The combined multi-stage battery was attempted twice but stalled while entering
